cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >
  If you use this software or reproducibility package, please cite it using the
  metadata below.
type: software
title: >
  Federated Learning for Resource-Aware Intrusion Detection in IoT Networks:
  An Empirical Study of IID and Device-Level Non-IID Data — Reproducibility Package
authors:
  - family-names: Azam
    given-names: Moazzam
    email: moazzamkk13@gmail.com
abstract: >
  This is the reproducibility package for a controlled empirical study comparing
  four training conditions (Centralized, Controlled IID FedAvg, Device-Level
  Non-IID FedAvg, and Local-Only) for binary botnet intrusion detection on the
  N-BaIoT dataset. The package includes the complete experiment codebase, frozen
  data split specifications, a persisted StandardScaler, publication figures and
  tables, the full research manuscript, and a comprehensive reproducibility guide.
  Experiments use a lightweight SmallMLP (9,537 parameters) evaluated across
  9 IoT device types (7,062,606 total observations, 115 features) on CPU with a
  single random seed (42) and a 3-round federated training horizon.
  The study is a pre-print and has not yet been peer-reviewed.
version: 1.0.0
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/Moazzam9/federated-iot-ids
keywords:
  - federated learning
  - IoT intrusion detection
  - N-BaIoT
  - FedAvg
  - non-IID data
  - device heterogeneity
  - empirical evaluation
  - botnet detection
  - reproducibility
